error_signature: "packaged default database missing|unable to open rgb database \"/[a-z]|install.*<pkg>.*<pkg>/share"
root_cause: "Conan's Autotools.install() installs via --destdir=<package_folder>, so every install directory coming from configure (--prefix and any explicitly absolute --with-*-dir) is treated as a path RELATIVE to the destination root and gets the package_folder prefixed onto it. When a recipe simultaneously bakes an absolute runtime path into the binary (to make a compiled-in default data location work) the two mechanisms fight: the data file lands at <pkg>/<pkg>/share/... instead of <pkg>/share/..., so the binary's compiled-in default can never be satisfied and the packaged data file appears to be missing."
rec_approach: "Keep the baked runtime path pointing at the final in-package location (self.package_folder is already known in generate()), and in package() relocate the installed data file back to the canonical path under package_folder, then prune the duplicated absolute-path shell directory created by the destdir overlap. Do not try to solve it by making the baked path relative - the compiled-in string must match the file's real location at run time."
match_keywords: ["destdir", "Autotools.install", "package_folder", "absolute install directory", "duplicated nested path", "data file missing", "compiled-in default path", "relocate"]
error_excerpt: "FAIL: packaged default database missing: <CONAN_HOME>/p/b/rgbXXXX/p/share/X11/rgb.txt  (实际被 make install 放到 <CONAN_HOME>/p/b/rgbXXXX/p/storage/Users/.../p/share/X11/rgb.txt)"
severity: P1
category: packaging
last_updated: 2026-09-23
